{
  "info": {
    "sylid": 6713,
    "subjectCode": "SSP201",
    "syllabusName": "Pitching creative ideas_Nghệ thuật thuyết phục và bán ý tưởng",
    "syllabusEnglish": "Pitching creative ideas",
    "credits": "3",
    "degreeLevel": "Bachelor",
    "timeAllocation": "Study hour (150h)\n\n= 45h contact hours + 105h self-study",
    "prerequisite": "None",
    "description": "Description: This course helps students to persuade employers, sell ideas to investors and pitch a client for new business. The course also introduces students to the tools and techniques they will need to convince people. For more details, it introduces and examines the STRONG method of pitching, which can be put to use immediately: Setting the Frame, Telling the Story, Revealing the Intrigue, Offering the Prize, Nailing the Hookpoint and Getting a Decision.\n\nLecturer will use several teaching methods such as conducting group discussion and sharing field work experiences in the market on top of regular teaching. Students will have the chance to showcase their presentation and persuasion skills as well as their thinking process related to this field.\n\nTeaching methods: Direct Instruction, Inquiry-based Learning, Cooperative Learning, Case Study Analysis",
    "studentTasks": "- Students must attend more than 80% of contact slots in order to be accepted to the final examination.\n\n- Student is responsible to do all exercises, assignments and labs given by instructor in class or at home and submit on time\n\n- Use laptop in class only for learning purpose\n\n- Promptly access to the FU CMS at http://cms.fpt.edu.vn for up-to-date course information",
    "tools": "- Textbook\n\n- Computer",
