      "duration": null,
      "clo": "LO1, LO2, LO3, LO4, LO5, LO6, LO7, LO8, LO9",
      "questionType": "Option 1: Group Presentation,Group Report; Option 2: (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal",
      "noQuestion": "N/A",
      "knowledgeSkill": "Option 1: Test the acquainted knowledge which student obtained in the class; Option 2: (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal",
      "gradingGuide": "Option 1:\n\nStudents assume they are working for an agency/big corporate and responsible for come up with an idea based on the goal(s) decided by lecturer. This practice is intended to help students to pitch their ideas in order to convince their client/boss that their ideas are worthy and valuable.\n\nFor the report, the idea pitch must include at least:\n\n(1) The goal(s)\n\n(2) Target audiences: stakeholders and the end user\n\n(3) The big idea\n\n(4) Key message(s)\n\n(5) The 4 phases\n\n(6) Evaluation and discussion (the potential of your ideas)\n\nRequirements:\n\nThe presentation should adhere to the following guidelines:\n\n1. Time limit imposed must be met.\n\n2. All team members must actively participate in the pitch.\n\n3. Presentation should be of professional standard.\n\n4. Pitching theories should be used.\n\nNote:\n\nPresentations are assessed on the skills explored and developed in the course, including choice of material suited to length and audience, rhetorical structure, use of voice and body, engagement and interaction with audience, and tone and style.\n\nOption 2: (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal",
      "note": "Option 1:\n\nThe mark will be given based on each student's performance in class, not on the whole group's. It means each student will get their own mark.\n\nPresentation (20) + Report (10%)\n\nOption 2: (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal"
    },
