      "knowledgeSkill": "Option 1: Test the acquainted knowledge which student obtained in the class; Option 2: (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal",
      "gradingGuide": "Option 1:\n\nStudents will be required to pick an advertisement and analyze the advertisement through the lens of one or more of the persuasion theories discussed in class.\n\nThis practice is intended to help students identify basic concepts and principles of pitching ideas effectively by analysing a key development, change or issue applied to the field of pitching ideas. Through the advertisement, students will learn how to convey their idea to convince their stakeholders.\n\nStudents will choose a topic from the list provided by the lecturer, or they may provide a detailed topic of their own to be cleared in writing by the lecturer. The topics are intended to justify some of the themes covered in the course and provide them with the opportunity to gain insights into the art of expressing ideas.\n\nRequirements:\n\nThe presentation should adhere to the following guidelines:\n\n1. Time limit imposed must be met.\n\n2. All team members must actively participate in the pitch.\n\n3. Presentation should be of professional standard.\n\nType: Group Presentation\n\nWeight: 15%\n\nLength: 10-15 minutes/group\n\nOption 2: (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal",
